">",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"3eb8af89f637d21b","after":"dc4d70d4239dea9c"}},"payload":{"text":"The shell chrome. Owns the shell hub and, once mounted, links it to the app iframe, mounts the review panel into\nthe aside, and starts the features.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:31.080Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:31.080Z"}
{"id":"9946ecf8-f120-4f73-b4a3-8437ba030b05","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b9de40e8b56c97fd","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"7a8983dc2c58c7be8f755b7c8c9a6b97bf6ebb3b","start":6487,"end":6528},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","appAddress","=","new","URL","(","location",".","href",")"]},"context":{"before":"fffe07d037926e17","after":"3ca28dc6a9b0be59"}},"payload":{"text":"(without an instance's name: that says \"the top of one\", and the app finds it by looking up: shared/instance.ts)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:18.549Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:18.549Z"}
{"id":"a2ddbe01-e93e-4db2-96c8-e75fb00ceeea","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7e6227bd52df3347#1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"9569f00145f41161393a2950622666bdf4dabc7d","start":8802,"end":8811},"shape":{"type":"Identifier","atoms":["useEffect"]},"context":{"before":"156ce54bffa2d2b2","after":"97c66df91dabde91"}},"payload":{"text":"Apply the pane's width to wa-page's CSS var (collapsed → the rail's). Clamp against the live max so a narrow viewport\ncan't leave it wider than the editor. Inline `setProperty` wins over the static `.wa-shell` defaults.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:05.931Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:05.931Z"}
{"id":"a48773d3-ca10-4560-8f29-3fb1284a1bcf","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7d4638dafa3a894f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"ec816c2f8e54d970ea44e52ef934b1371f7b2091","start":31,"end":86},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","VsCodeColors","}","from","\"","theme/vscode-colors","\""]},"context":{"after":"779b9e943e48c349"}},"payload":{"text":"The outer SHELL — the app's main layout, built on Web Awesome's `<wa-page>` app-shell (header / main / aside), so the\nchrome is components + theme tokens with almost no hand-rolled layout CSS.\n\nWhen index.html loads at the TOP level, main.tsx calls `renderShell()` (dynamically, so this WA chunk never loads in\nthe editor iframe). It renders the chrome and iframes THIS same page back into the `main` region; that nested\ninstance sees `window.parent !== window` and takes the app branch, booting the workbench into it (fill mode). One\nentry, one bundle; the shell↔app seam is the hub.\n\nThis is the shell's core: the page, the dock the editor iframe is the fixed panel of, the shell hub linked to the app,\nthe theme, and the RHS review panel (git-panel.tsx, Web Awesome components of its own) in the `aside` region. Every\nother part of the top window is a feature (feature.ts): started once the hub is linked, its control placed in the top\nbar, what it draws over the page drawn — FEATURES, below, is the list.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:46.057Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:46.057Z"}
{"id":"abfd3ba9-01ab-46d7-8bdc-40212cbb1ad7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"879dc70a3d3318a6","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"78b72786240878d31f421ce1bb2ce82404b2b1e2","start":3712,"end":3733},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","RAIL_WIDTH","=","68"]},"context":{"before":"32f8d0fa514ff58b","after":"4c9860b7471c9197"}},"payload":{"text":"A collapsed pane isn't hidden — it becomes a slim RAIL (WebAwesome vertical social-share pattern): a pill card\nwith a stacked icon-button + tiny caption that reopens the pane. This is the region's width when collapsed.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:36.198Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:36.198Z"}
{"id":"b082733c-f3e6-4473-b258-514ea02ad11d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2fd72e5b9670a095","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"4621890a636840380a0ff133431e25df93fcffaa","start":6827,"end":6862},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["relayLoggerToHub","(","shellHub",",","\"","shell","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"5d2e44a338d3e942","after":"9a40fe2c17c2f02c"}},"payload":{"text":"…and its logs and spans (the GitHub data plane's, a repository's load, the reset's), on `$sys.log.shell`, and its\nuncaught errors: debug-mcp and the monitor see the shell as they see every other context.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:16.054Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:16.054Z"}
{"id":"e0dc5d23-3bcc-4c80-a247-c3119db61389","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"32f8d0fa514ff58b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"67bd2a7ecd4c756579662072ff3e50085f323262","start":3360,"end":3599},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","loadPaneWidth","(","key",":","string",",","fallback",":","number",")",":","number","{","try","{","const","value","=","Number","(","localStorage",".","getItem","(","\"","shell:","\"","+","key",")",")",";","return","Number",".","isFinite","(","value",")","&&","value",">","0","?","value",":","fallback",";","}","catch","{","return","fallback",";","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"5fbcf0d55bf2a1cf","after":"879dc70a3d3318a6"}},"payload":{"text":"A persisted pane width, clamped later against the live max. Falls back to the default if unset/invalid.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:38.631Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:38.631Z"}
{"id":"e385e823-88bc-4533-a45a-cb005a5f6d48","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6297c8c07a0ebdfa","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"34656d77df9e586da731d578de6fd46a41f01154","start":10253,"end":10586},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","onResizeKey","=","(","event",":","KeyboardEvent",")",":","void","=>","{","if","(","event",".","key","!==","\"","ArrowLeft","\"","&&","event",".","key","!==","\"","ArrowRight","\"",")","{","return",";","}","event",".","preventDefault","(",")",";","const","nudge","=","event",".","key","===","\"","ArrowLeft","\"","?","16",":","-","16",";","const","max","=","paneMax","(",")",";","setAsideWidth","(","(","value",")","=>","Math",".","max","(","PANE",".","asideMin",",","Math",".","min","(","max",",","value","+","nudge",")",")",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"47d9531ff5bb8124","after":"6d44d4dbfedf04fa"}},"payload":{"text":"Keyboard resize (the grip is a focusable separator): arrows nudge by 16px — the pane grows leftward, as it's dragged.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:38:55.965Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:38:55.965Z"}
{"id":"e39d2031-8758-4b95-9407-65b82d64daef","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7e6227bd52df3347#2","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"827e7984a85976b0d5556c153cb5e2e8040fc292","start":9214,"end":9223},"shape":{"type":"Identifier","atoms":["useEffect"]},"context":{"before":"d3c192f1480fe9d2","after":"565e56f4c37816ba"}},"payload":{"text":"Persist the width so it survives reloads (per browser; localStorage may be unavailable in private mode).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:03.435Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:03.435Z"}
{"id":"f0e08f23-86b9-4800-867e-74632b863773","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3eb8af89f637d21b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"bf67cab692870b1f12195188556804cbdf80ae06","start":4090,"end":4543},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","RailContent","(","{","items","}",":","{","\"","items","\"",":","RailItem","[]","}",")","{","return","(","<",">","\n\t\t\t","{","items",".","map","(","(","item",")","=>","(","<","span","key","=","{","item",".","label","}","class","=","\"","wa-stack wa-gap-3xs wa-align-items-center","\"",">","\n\t\t\t\t\t","<","wa-button","appearance","=","\"","plain","\"","variant","=","\"","neutral","\"","size","=","\"","small","\"","pill","title","=","{","item",".","title","}","aria-label","=","{","item",".","title","}","onClick","=","{","item",".","onClick","}",">","<","Icon","node","=","{","item",".","node","}","/>","</","wa-button",">","\n\n\t\t\t\t\t","<","span","class","=","\"","wa-caption-3xs wa-text-center","\"",">","{","item",".","label","}","</","span",">","\n\t\t\t\t","</","span",">",")",")","}","\n\t\t","</",">",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"4c9860b7471c9197","after":"ae7adc7b8a69208f"}},"payload":{"text":"A collapsed pane's rail: a bare vertical stack of pill icon-buttons with captions (no card). Rendered as a\nfragment straight into the pane's slot region so the region's other content (the imperatively-mounted git panel)\ncan stay mounted-but-hidden across collapse.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:33.636Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:33.636Z"}
{"id":"f8769da2-6a15-4ec3-a9f6-e20309a2e1d6","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"969ec38cd7cdd040","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"00c13b11ec42d210d6065655896a9605367aba8c","start":7835,"end":7853},"shape":{"type":"MemberExpression","atoms":["shellHub",".","subscribe"]},"context":{"before":"0f9f1df0567619b4","after":"3b7a97c559bfcd96"}},"payload":{"text":"And the shell draws in VS Code's colours, as the editor publishes them (theme/vscode-colors): the top bar, the panels and their popovers read as VS Code's.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:11.038Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:39:11.038Z"}
{"id":"731b866b-3dd2-488f-885b-dafc81867a76","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b218d21d91470908","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/shell.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"9e78cd1fa34fbe0e756e2ab20e20a4a71123ca8d","start":1655,"end":1676},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","\"","theme/chrome","\""]},"context":{"before":"890006c0458b915e","after":"14392047dce81fa3"}},"payload":{"text":"Web Awesome (not its native styles), our brand tokens, the system's light/dark mode","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T19:09:05.316Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T19:09:05.316Z"}
